cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MEMORIA in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MEMORIA: Long-Horizon Memory Intelligence & Reliability Observatory"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/soyebmohammad03-dev/MEMORIA"
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammad
    given-names: Soyeb
abstract: >-
  MEMORIA is a reproducible laboratory for studying artificial memory over long interaction
  horizons: formation, retrieval, consolidation, forgetting, interference, contradiction and
  belief revision, calibrated uncertainty, adaptive importance, replay and provenance-based
  autopsy. Memory systems are the subject of controlled experiments on generated worlds, with
  content-addressed records, paired statistics and reproduction from manifests.
keywords:
  - artificial memory
  - long-horizon agents
  - belief revision
  - calibration
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - retrieval
  - forgetting
